      "message": "I am 100% against adding in options like this. We can\u0027t ever make it default False and no one except edge cases will opt in to it. This \"fix\" still feels like a change for speculative benefits.\n\nIf we are doing this we should be looking at how we can handle the current uses while maintaining the efficiency gains. I also would like to have clear proof of these efficiency gains. \n\nSorry to be hard on this proposal but I\u0027m not convinced this is a win due to both added complexity and the relative edge case it is solving. The tokens being stored in the DB is soon to be the non-recommended method, moving to Fernet removes the bulk of data that keystone has to manage in the DB. I would rather see focus on the rolling schema migrations and other SQL-specific [fix the joins, stop hitting the db 400000 times for the same object in the same request] than muck with the datatypes in the schema for the sake of minor index efficiency gains and minor storage gains.",
